LZ-DSO, the Landing Zone DevSecOps secure code development environment, was one of the internal systems whose passwords were exposed, and the Artifactory package repository credentials were a separate item in the archive. CISA said there was no indication that sensitive data was compromised and that it was adding safeguards; the staffing loss of nearly a third of its workforce is Krebs's context, not a CISA statement about contractor oversight. The work-to-home synchronization is Caturegli's suspicion, and his backdoor scenario for the Artifactory credentials is a risk assessment, not a finding of write access.
